  - gpu
  - sustainability
  - systems-research
  - frontier
abstract: >
  ThermalShift demonstrates that persistent machine-level thermal differences
  on the Frontier supercomputer can be converted into a workload-placement signal.
  Across 30 matched historical-replay Monte Carlo scenarios, fingerprint-aware
  scheduling (FP-cap-10) outperformed thermally unaware random placement in all 30
  scenarios. Among 29 uncensored scenarios, the median paired feasible-capacity
  advantage was +15.5 percentage points (bootstrap 95% CI: +11.5 to +21.9 pp).
